From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mattyperrott <mattyperrott@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a home-screen widget

For the copy of Fauxx built into Virtroid's cloud phones (VIRTROID.md).
The widget fills the home screen's width and two rows (on Android 12+,
resized to one row, a compact layout): whether the engine is generating
decoy activity or why it is paused, a switch that starts or stops it as
the notification's Start and the dashboard's switch do (before the
consent dialog has been accepted it opens the app instead), every decoy
action Fauxx has made, and its hourly rate over the last day, as the
dashboard counts it. A "?" opens the FAQ. System fonts and Virtroid's
palette (dark, with a lime accent), so it pairs with the other widgets
on Virtroid's home screen; on Android 12+ its switch is the system's
own, drawn in those colours.

PhantomForegroundService publishes each state it puts in its
notification to the widget (updateNotification is synchronized so the
60s tick and the state collector can't post an older state after a
newer one), PoisonEngine counts each action it records for it, and
Settings' "Clear All Data" forgets that count. MainActivity takes the
widget's "?" and the navigation graph opens the FAQ for it.

The About screen says the build is modified and links to its source,
and the version name is 0.9.3-virtroid.2.
