+# Virtroid's changes to Fauxx
+
+This is Fauxx 0.9.3 (<https://github.com/digital-grease/fauxx>, tag `v0.9.3`,
+commit `1598ac1e5813d06079da4f65ab6392970c4e3f43`) as modified by Virtroid on
+2 and 3 November 2026, for the copy of Fauxx built into Virtroid's cloud phones.
+Like Fauxx, it is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
+version 3 only (`LICENSE`).
+
+The changes:
+
+- A home-screen widget (`app/src/main/java/com/fauxx/widget`, its layout,
+  provider info, drawables and strings), the full width of the home screen
+  and two rows tall (on Android 12+ a compact layout at one row): whether the engine is generating decoy activity or why it is paused, a
+  switch that starts or stops it as the notification's Start and the
+  dashboard's switch do (before the consent dialog has been accepted it
+  opens the app instead), every decoy action Fauxx has made, and its hourly
+  rate over the last day, as the dashboard counts it. A "?" opens the FAQ.
+  It shows no persona, categories or log.
+- `PhantomForegroundService` publishes the state it shows in its
+  notification to the widget (`updateNotification` is synchronized, so the
+  60s tick and the state collector can't post an older state after a
+  newer one), and `PoisonEngine` counts each action it records for it.
+  Settings' "Clear All Data" forgets that count too.
+- `MainActivity` takes the widget's "?" (`EXTRA_OPEN_FAQ`) and the navigation
+  graph opens the FAQ for it.
+- The widget takes the system's fonts and Virtroid's palette (dark, with a
+  lime accent), so it pairs with the other widgets on Virtroid's home
+  screen; on Android 12+ its switch is the system's own, drawn in those
+  colours, and before that a drawn one.
+- The About screen says that this build is modified and links to its
+  source.
+- The version name is `0.9.3-virtroid.2`; the version code is upstream's.
+
+Virtroid builds it with `./gradlew assembleFullRelease` (JDK 21, Android SDK
+platform 37) and signs it with Virtroid's release key. The build script, this
+change as a patch against the tag, and where each build's complete source is
+published are in <https://github.com/mattyperrott/Virtroid/tree/main/deploy/aosp/apps/fauxx>.
